The screenshots show that although the `<Dropdown>` container is receiving the `--light` modifier (via the wrapper’s `className`), the inner `<ListBox>` never sees the `light` prop—so it never renders the `bx--list-box--light` class. In other words, the `light` flag is dropped in `Dropdown.js` and never forwarded to the `ListBox` component.

Below is a single patch that fixes this by passing `light={light}` through to `<ListBox>`.

```javascript
### packages/react/src/components/Dropdown/Dropdown.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
            <ListBox
              id={id}
              type={type}
              className={className({ isOpen })}
              disabled={disabled}
              isOpen={isOpen}
              invalid={invalid}
              invalidText={invalidText}
              {...getRootProps({ refKey: 'innerRef' })}>
=======
            <ListBox
              id={id}
              type={type}
              light={light}
              className={className({ isOpen })}
              disabled={disabled}
              isOpen={isOpen}
              invalid={invalid}
              invalidText={invalidText}
              {...getRootProps({ refKey: 'innerRef' })}>
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

With this change, when you pass `light` into `<Dropdown light>`, the underlying `<ListBox>` will also render with the `bx--list-box--light` class as expected.
